## P1: correctness bugs that produce wrong output silently

### 5. Use the real source pixel format
Assessment 3.4. `videodecoder.cpp:65`: replace `AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P` with
`m_codecCtx->pix_fmt`. Currently masked by hardware decode not engaging (item 7).
Est: 15 min. Test with a 10-bit or yuv422p clip.

### 6. Fix `QWaitCondition` misuse
Assessment 3.7. `videodecoder.cpp:135`. Lock `m_mutex` before `m_cond.wait()`, or
replace the pause path with a `QSemaphore`. This is undefined behavior on every
pause, currently unreported because it does not always crash.
Est: 30 min.

### 7. Decide on hardware decode: fix it or drop the claim
Assessment 3.5. Either install a `get_format` callback so hwaccel actually engages
(and then item 5 becomes load-bearing, since D3D11VA downloads as NV12), or remove
`initHardwareDecoder()` and stop claiming it in README and PRD.
Est: 3 hours to fix properly, 10 min to drop the claim honestly.

### 8. Wire `applySaturation` or remove the CO
Assessment 3.3. It is one line in `paintEvent`, next to the existing
`applyBrightnessContrast` call. Do not leave a live CO that does nothing.
Est: 15 min.

### 9. Fix or remove `setSpeed`
Assessment 3.3. Dead method. Either drive it from the deck rate CO or delete it.
Est: 15 min.

### 10. Stop duplicating COs in the fullscreen window
Assessment 3.8. `slotVideoFullscreen` constructs a second `VideoWidget` on the same
group. Add a render-only mode, or a separate lightweight frame-display widget that
does not register controls.
Est: 1 hour.

