## P2: exporters, currently wired to guaranteed failure

### 11. Pass the deck's actual track path, not the group string
Assessment 3.9. `export_controls.cpp:44-51`. Resolve the loaded track for the group
via `PlayerManager` / `BaseTrackPlayer::getLoadedTrack()`, then pass
`pTrack->getLocation()`.
Est: 1 hour.

### 12. Pass a real crate name
Assessment 3.9. `export_controls.cpp:60` passes `QString()`. Needs a crate selection
mechanism. ControlObjects hold doubles only, so a `[Export],rekordbox_usb_path`
string CO as documented in README is not possible. Either add a small preferences
UI or a config-file setting.
Est: 3 hours with a minimal dialog.

### 13. Rename the Rekordbox exporter to what it is
Assessment 3.10. libdjinterop writes Engine Library, not Pioneer DeviceSQL.
Rename `RekordboxExporter` to `EngineExporter`, change the target directory from
`PIONEER/rekordbox` to `Engine Library/`, update COs and docs. The feature becomes
correct and useful instead of silently producing a USB stick no CDJ will read.

If Pioneer export is genuinely wanted later, that is a separate project against the
DeviceSQL format, not a config change.
Est: 2 hours for the rename, plus doc updates.

### 14. Fix hot cue type filter
Assessment 3.11. `rekordboxexporter.cpp:196`: `cr.type == 2` should be
`cr.type == 1`. `cueinfo.h:12-14` is the authority.
Est: 5 min. Cover it in the exporter test.

### 15. Do not recreate the database per track
Assessment 3.12. Refactor `exportCrate` to open the Engine DB once and loop
`create_track`, rather than calling `exportTrack` per row.
Est: 1 hour.

### 16. Make the export destination explicit
Assessment 3.13. Replace the volume-size heuristic in `defaultExportPath()` with an
explicit user-chosen path. Current logic can select an SD card or a mounted ISO and
write into it.
Est: 1 hour with a folder picker.

### 17. Write `exporter_test.cpp`
Seed a temp SQLite with the Mixxx schema, export one track, assert the output has
the right track count and hot cues. Catches items 11, 14, 15 permanently.
Est: 2 hours.

